  "evidence_notes": "Diagnosed with Crohn's 15 years ago, also has chronic migraines and fibromyalgia. Initial treatments (prednisone, mesalamine, azathioprine) failed or caused adverse reactions. Biologics started early (Remicade at 24), worked for 4 years, then failed during pregnancy. Switched to Humira post-pregnancy, which worked for 3 years. After Humira failure and insurance denial of Cimzia, patient started Stelara 2 years ago. Treatment is ongoing but symptoms persist, with the primary goal being to avoid surgery. Patient is a single mother struggling with fatigue, financial burdens, and the challenges of dating. She finds support in therapy and online groups."
